# OpenClaw .env example
#
# Quick start:
# 1) Copy this file to `.env` (for local runs from this repo), OR to `~/.openclaw/.env` (for launchd/systemd daemons).
# 2) Fill only the values you use.
# 3) Keep real secrets out of git.
#
# Env-source precedence for environment variables (highest -> lowest):
# process env, ./.env, ~/.openclaw/.env, then openclaw.json `env` block.
# Existing non-empty process env vars are not overridden by dotenv/config env loading.
# Note: direct config keys (for example `gateway.auth.token` or channel tokens in openclaw.json)
# are resolved separately from env loading and often take precedence over env fallbacks.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gateway auth + paths
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required if the gateway binds beyond loopback. Leave blank to have OpenClaw
# auto-generate a token on first start, or provide your own using
# `openssl rand -hex 32`. The gateway will refuse to start if this is set to
# the documented example placeholder, so never copy-paste an example value
# from docs or tutorials into this file verbatim.
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN=

# Optional alternative auth mode (use token OR password).
# OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_PASSWORD=

# Optional path overrides (defaults shown for reference).
# OPENCLAW_STATE_DIR=~/.openclaw
# OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=~/.openclaw/openclaw.json
# OPENCLAW_HOME=~
# Docker setup stores auth profile encryption key material outside the mounted
# OpenClaw state dir and mounts this host directory into the container.
# OPENCLAW_AUTH_PROFILE_SECRET_DIR=/absolute/path/to/.openclaw-auth-profile-secrets

# Allowlist of extra directories that `$include` directives in openclaw.json may
# resolve files from. Path-list separated (':' on POSIX, ';' on Windows). Each
# entry is tilde-expanded. Without this, `$include` is confined to the directory
# containing openclaw.json.
# OPENCLAW_INCLUDE_ROOTS=/etc/openclaw/shared:~/.openclaw/shared

# Optional: import missing keys from your login shell profile.
# OPENCLAW_LOAD_SHELL_ENV=1
# OPENCLAW_SHELL_ENV_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model provider API keys (set at least one)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# OPENCLAW_LIVE_OPENAI_KEY=sk-...
# OPENCLAW_LIVE_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-...
# OPENCLAW_LIVE_GEMINI_KEY=...
# OPENAI_API_KEY_1=...
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_1=...
# GEMINI_API_KEY_1=...
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...
# OPENAI_API_KEYS=sk-1,sk-2
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEYS=sk-ant-1,sk-ant-2
# GEMINI_API_KEYS=key-1,key-2

# Optional additional providers
# ZAI_API_KEY=...
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=...
# TOKENHUB_API_KEY=...
# LKEAP_API_KEY=...
# MINIMAX_API_KEY=...
# SYNTHETIC_API_KEY=...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Channels (only set what you enable)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456:ABCDEF...
# DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=...
# SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
# SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...

# Optional channel env fallbacks
# MATTERMOST_BOT_TOKEN=...
# MATTERMOST_URL=https://chat.example.com
# ZALO_BOT_TOKEN=...
# OPENCLAW_TWITCH_ACCESS_TOKEN=oauth:...

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tools + voice/media (optional)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BRAVE_API_KEY=...
# PERPLEXITY_API_KEY=pplx-...
# FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=...

# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=...
# XI_API_KEY=...  # alias for ElevenLabs
# INWORLD_API_KEY=...
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=...

# =============================================================================
# Deploy / docker-compose (this fork's additions — not in upstream openclaw)
# =============================================================================
# Consumed by docker-compose.yml + docker-compose.override.yml + Dockerfile.minimus.

# Image tag the compose stack uses. Build target for `docker compose build`.
OPENCLAW_IMAGE=openclaw:local

# Loopback bind interfaces for the gateway/bridge. The override forces 127.0.0.1
# regardless, but the port numbers come from here.
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_PORT=18789
OPENCLAW_BRIDGE_PORT=18790

# Bind mode passed to `node dist/index.js gateway --bind`. `lan` lets clients on
# the SSH tunnel hit the gateway; `loopback` is stricter but blocks tunneled use.
OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_BIND=lan

# Host paths for openclaw state + workspace. Bind-mounted into the container.
# Use absolute paths — `~` is not expanded by docker-compose env interpolation.
OPENCLAW_CONFIG_DIR=/home/ubuntu/.openclaw
OPENCLAW_WORKSPACE_DIR=/home/ubuntu/.openclaw/workspace

# Used by the `gog` skill (Gmail) for its OS keyring. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
GOG_KEYRING_PASSWORD=

# jira-cli API token. Server/email/project key live in deploy/jira/config.yml
# (baked into the image at /etc/jira/.config.yml). Create a token at
# https://id.atlassian.com/manage-profile/security/api-tokens and paste below.
JIRA_API_TOKEN=

# SHA256 checksums for skill binaries are baked into Dockerfile.minimus as
# ARG defaults — no operator action needed unless upgrading binary versions.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SearXNG self-hosted web search (this fork's addition)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The `searxng` service in docker-compose.prod.yml provides key-free web
# search to the bundled openclaw `searxng` extension plugin. Service is
# internal-only on the compose network; gateway reaches it at
# http://searxng:8080. See deploy/searxng/README.md for the matching
# openclaw.json snippet to apply on EC2.

# Cookie/session signing key. The searxng image's entrypoint substitutes
# this into /etc/searxng/settings.yml at startup. Generate once:
#   echo "SEARXNG_SECRET=$(openssl rand -hex 32)" >> .env
SEARXNG_SECRET=

# Build-arg list of bundled plugins to KEEP in dist/extensions when the
# gateway image is built. Dockerfile defaults to "" — anything listed in
# package.json's `!dist/extensions/<id>/**` exclude block (acpx, brave,
# bluebubbles, codex, diagnostics-otel, diffs, discord, feishu, googlechat,
# google-meet, line, lobster, memory-lancedb, msteams, nextcloud-talk,
# nostr, qqbot, synology-chat, tlon, twitch, voice-call, whatsapp, zalo,
# zalouser, and the qa-* test surfaces) is pruned from the runtime image
# unless you name it here. If `openclaw plugins list` doesn't show an
# extension you need (and `ls /app/dist/extensions/<id>/` returns ENOENT),
# add the id below and `dcp build openclaw-gateway && dcp up -d openclaw-gateway`.
#
# - searxng: web_search provider (deploy/searxng/)
# - codex:   agent harness; needed when `agents.defaults.harness = "codex"`
#            or any agent uses `harness: "codex"` — the canonical symptom
#            is `Requested agent harness "codex" is not registered.`
#
# Affects `dcp build` only — `dcp up -d` without a build does not change
# the image. Verify after rebuild:
#   dcp exec openclaw-gateway ls /app/dist/extensions/ | grep -E 'searxng|codex'
OPENCLAW_EXTENSIONS=searxng,codex

# Optional uWSGI tuning (defaults: 2 workers x 4 threads).
# SEARXNG_UWSGI_WORKERS=2
# SEARXNG_UWSGI_THREADS=4
